            <ArticleTitle>[Health status of the workers exposed to strong, constant magnetic fields].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>65-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Forty two workers underwent examinations under clinical conditions. The workers were affected by the magnetic field of intensities ranging between 112-190 Gauss, depending on the workplace. They underwent internal, ophthalmological, psychological, psychiatric and analytical examinations and the health status of those exposed was compared to that of twenty controls. Most subjects, mainly those of long length of employment in e-m fields exposure, exhibited nonspecific abdominal pains, general weakness, insomnia, increased thirst and conjunctivitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
